WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.700
Hey, welcome to Models and Agents, episode 63 on May 29, 2026. Let's see what shipped.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.160
Let's see what happened in the AI world today. And trust me, it's been busy.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:20.460
Anthropic's $65 billion series age at $965 billion valuation and $47 billion run rate revenue

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:25.740
show Claude demand is scaling faster than most labs can match. Liquid AI shipped

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:33.420
LFM 2.58B A1B with 128K context after 38 trillion pre-training tokens.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:42.340
A model kernel on 8 AMD MI 300X cards reached 3,300 output tokens per second on small models.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:50.340
Researchers also dropped right now Arabic 0.5B turbo and Arya Bata 2, while local builders

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:57.780
mode agents toward direct HTML rendering. Anthropic announced a $65 billion series age round

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:04.160
at a $965 billion post-money valuation. The round was led by Altimeter,

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:10.520
Dragonear, Green Oaks, and Sequoia. The company separately reported that run rate revenue crossed

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:17.920
$47 billion earlier this month from enterprise Claude deployments. The new capital will expand

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:23.540
research and inference capacity. The round highlights how quickly production usage of frontier

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:32.920
models is growing across industries. Liquid AI released LFM 2.58B A1B as an edge-focused model.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:43.160
It expands the prior LFM 2A B1B with a 128K context window and 38 trillion tokens of pre-training

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:48.480
plus large-scale reinforcement learning. The model doubles the vocabulary to improve

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:55.480
non-latent tokenization and supports tool-chaining on entry-level laptops. It is available now on

00:01:55.480 --> 00:02:04.580
hugging face. Right now, Arabic 0.5B turbo is a 518 million parameter Arabic specialized decoder.

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:14.060
It was built on twin 2.5 0.5B by adding 27,032 Arabic tokens and continued pre-training on

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:22.220
504 million Arabic tokens. The model reaches 35.9% mean accuracy on Arabic COPA,

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:30.340
Heliswag and MMLU benchmarks. The quantized build runs at 635 tokens per second on a single

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:38.940
H100. Ariobata 2 is a reasoning-focused model post-trained from GPT OSS 20B via reinforcement

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:46.260
learning on physics-wala question banks. It all performs the base model on JEEE main, JEEE

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:56.560
advanced, NEET, AIME and GPQA while using up to 64% fewer output tokens. The training combined

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:04.180
prolonged reinforcement learning with larger rollout groups. Users report Gemma 426 BA4B

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:10.460
running well on M5 Pro hardware. It shows strong generalist performance across creative writing,

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:17.380
debugging, image classification, and tool augmented chat. The model uses less memory than twin

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:25.920
3.635 BA3B while displaying more personality. A coding agent setup now renders responses directly

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:33.180
as HTML in the browser. Switching the system prompt from markdown to HTML improved diagram

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:42.420
quality and structure with inline SVGs, tables, and diagrams. The approach works with twin 3.627B

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:49.680
and requires only a simple prompt change plus a web UI. A new model kernel runs the full

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:57.520
decode sequence as one GPU resident program on 8 times MI 300X. It maps memory access to

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:04.460
die topology and achieves up to 3,300 output tokens per second per request at batch size 1

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:10.260
with no quantization. The team plans future support for large mixture of experts models.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:16.740
A Laura-based method uses hidden state probes to teach models to verbalize their actual confidence.

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:23.640
The approach works across 7B to 70B models from four families with only a few hundred examples

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:30.340
and under 10 minutes on an M3 Ultra. Activation patching confirms the effect is causal.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:39.240
Early benchmarks on an M5 Max with 128GB show stepfund 3.7 Flash delivering usable speeds

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:48.700
at 32K to 64K context in Q4KS quantization. The model remains responsive below 16K context.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:58.280
Test LFM 2.58BA1. Be on a local laptop for tool chaining workflows, where 128K context

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:04.360
matters more than raw size. Switch an existing coding agent prompt to HTML output

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:09.180
and measure how quickly diagram rendering improves without extra post processing.

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:16.360
Run the probe-targeted Laura recipe on a 7B to 13B model you already use for agent decision

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:24.740
making to reduce overconfident errors. Benchmark stepfund 3.7 Flash against Gemma 426B

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:31.040
on your M series hardware for mixed creative and coding tasks. More teams are expected to release

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:36.060
small specialized models after the Arabic and SDEM examples shown today.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:43.220
Additional model kernel and single program inference work on AMD and Apple Silicon hardware is

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:49.840
likely as memory bandwidth remains the bottleneck. Continued experiments with HTML and structured

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:55.000
output formats for agents will appear as builders move away from markdown defaults.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:06:02.400
Okay, let's pop the hood on the probe-targeted fine-tuning approach. Everyone talks about LLM

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:08.520
confidence as a simple prompt fix and practice the model already encodes correctness signals in

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:18.020
its hidden states at 0.76 to 0.88AUROC. Yet surface text stays stuck at 99% because of training

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:24.460
dynamics. The method extracts those internal signals with linear probes then uses the probe outputs

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:31.380
as fine-tuning targets. This adds almost no inference cost after the short LLM and works across

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:37.920
model scales because the probe only needs to read one activation position. The quality gain is

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:45.060
largest on mid-sized models. At 70B the softmax already carries usable signal but the argmax

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:51.020
text still collapses. Activation patching at the exact confidence token moves the output

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:58.180
distribution with correlation 0.976. Apply it when you need the model to admit uncertainty on

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:05.240
factual or multi-step tasks. Skip it if your pipeline already filters low probability tokens downstream.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:11.760
The gacha that bites most teams is seed sensitivity in the shape of the confidence distribution

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:18.920
even when discrimination stays stable. Tomorrow keep an eye on more small specialized models

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:25.620
and further monocernal inference experiments on AMD hardware. That wraps up today's AI briefing.

